<% content_for :title, "Privacy | #{current_store.name}" %>

<div class="page stack" style="padding-top:var(--space-8);max-width:760px">
  <div class="card checkout__section">
    <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--accent" style="font-size:var(--fs-body-sm)">Privacy</p>
    <h1 style="font-size:var(--fs-display-3)">Privacy preferences</h1>
    <p class="sub">Choose whether this store can use analytics cookies for visit tracking and Meta Pixel events.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="card card--accent checkout__section">
    <%= button_to "Accept analytics", privacy_preferences_path,
          params: { analytics: PrivacyConsent::ACCEPTED },
          class: "btn btn--primary btn--lg btn--full" %>
    <%= button_to "Decline analytics", privacy_preferences_path,
          params: { analytics: PrivacyConsent::DECLINED },
          class: "btn btn--outline btn--lg btn--full" %>
  </div>

  <div class="card card--pad-lg legal">
    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>To take an order we need your name, email, postal address and phone number. Your card number is
       entered inside Stripe's own form and never reaches this store — we only ever see the last four
       digits and the result of the charge. If you pay with PayPal, PayPal tells us only that the
       payment succeeded.</p>
    <p>We also record what you looked at on the site, but only if you accepted analytics above.</p>

    <h2>Why we are allowed to</h2>
    <p>We process your order details because we need them to perform the contract you entered into.
       We keep records of sales because tax law requires it. Analytics and advertising measurement
       run on your consent, which you can withdraw at any time using the buttons above.</p>

    <h2>Who else sees it</h2>
    <p>Only the companies that make the order happen: our payment providers (Stripe, PayPal), our
       shipping and fulfilment partner, our email provider, and our hosting provider. Each sees only
       what its job requires. We do not sell your data, and we never will.</p>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>Order records are kept as long as tax law requires
       <mark class="legal__todo">(state the retention period for your country)</mark>. Analytics data
       is kept for 14 months. Anything else is deleted when it is no longer needed.</p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>You can ask us for a copy of what we hold, ask us to correct it, or ask us to delete it. Write to
       <%= mail_to current_store.support_email %> and we answer within 30 days. If you are not
       satisfied you can complain to your national data protection authority.</p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>The store sets a session cookie so your cart survives page loads — that one is essential and
       cannot be switched off. Analytics and Meta Pixel cookies are set only after you accept above.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p><mark class="legal__todo">Name the legal entity responsible for this data and its registered
       address; this is required by law in most jurisdictions.</mark>
       Questions: <%= mail_to current_store.support_email %>.</p>
  </div>
</div>
